@Author CameronPinchin

Personal project, generally for practicing C. 
Started because I wanted to try to restart SSHD on my Pi without plugging in a keyboard.
 - Couldn't connect via ssh to Pi.
 - Swiftly became aware that restarting sshd.service isn't going to fix the issue.
 - Continued anyways because its a good project.

This is essentially just a interface for systemctl commands, where the server is hosted on the RPi. 
The server receives datagrams from clients, that contain a service and an action. 
  i.e., "./<client_binary> <action> <service>"

The server then tries to run the corresponding command and let the client know if it succeeded or failed.
